ary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8104) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-11700K @ 3.60GHz (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using localization remaps on LabelSettings resources, this seems to work in the editor, however throws warnings and doesn't perform the remap in an exported project. The warning thrown doesn't make much sense as it first claims that the resource doesn't exist, then falls back to that same resource:\n\n```\nWARNING: Translation remap 'res://label_settings.tres' does not exist. Falling back to 'res://label_settings.tres'.\n     at: _path_remap (core/io/resource_loader.cpp:1273)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add two different label settings\n- In the Localization > Remaps tab of Project Settings, set up a remap that remaps one LabelSettings into another.\n- Add a Label in the world with the first LabelSettings\n- Export the project, you get an error when the Label loads.\n\n- In the repro project below, some Test text has been setup with a label settings, when pressing the French button, we swap the locale, and the Test text swaps to the international label settings variant that is coloured red, this uses a localization remap to swap the LabelSettings. Pressing English swaps back to English and makes the text white.\n- Export the project and play, now the buttons don't change the Test text colour and the error shown above is logged each time the language swaps or when the game starts.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[RemapBugTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24188293/RemapBugTest.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDO